  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 220 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nThe long term period is shaping up to be hot, dry and windy. \nSaturday, we start off in a weak ridging pattern with sunny skies \nand high temperatures forecast in the 90s. Sunday, we transition \ninto more of a zonal pattern for the remainder of the long term \nperiod. High temperatures are forecast in the 90s for the week with \nsome areas of the county warning area (CWA) reaching the 100s on \nMonday. Winds begin to pick up Sunday evening for our Colorado \ncounties with gusts around 30 mph possible. Overnight Sunday into \nMonday for the entire CWA with gusts from 20 to 40 mph possible. The \nwestern CWA will be on the higher end of wind gusts. Monday through \nWednesday, there is around a 20% chance of afternoon \nshowers/thunderstorms from embedded shortwave passages.",
